cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this hardware, please cite it as below."
title: "3DPLAM, 3D-Printed Lightweight Affordable Manifold for Microbial Water Quality Testing"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, 3D-printable membrane-filtration manifold for Escherichia coli
  quantification in drinking water, validated against the Millipore EZ-Fit
  stainless-steel manifold. Comprises a base, funnel and filter support, all
  printable without support structures on a consumer FDM printer.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-20
# The concept DOI, which always resolves to the newest version. It is the
# one to cite and the one in the README badge, so neither goes stale when
# a later release is archived. The DOI for this specific release is under
# identifiers below.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22025813
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22025814
    description: Archived record for version 1.0.0 specifically
# A single value, not a list: Zenodo takes one licence per record.
# The hardware in hardware/ is CERN-OHL-S v2, which is the more
# restrictive of the two and the one that governs the design itself;
# the documentation, data, site and tooling are CC BY 4.0, as set out
# in the README and in LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.md.
license: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
